  "disposition_rationale": "The batch protocol relies on air exposure for oxidation. In flow, mass transfer of oxygen from gas to liquid is the rate-limiting step for many photo-oxidations. While the batch yield is 99%, the flow residence time (5 min) is short. A 'SCREEN' disposition is appropriate because we must experimentally verify if the gas-liquid mass transfer in the selected coil is sufficient to achieve high conversion within the 5-minute residence time, or if a longer residence time or higher gas flow is required. The design is physically feasible and safe, but optimization is likely needed.",
  "proposal_json": "{\"residence_time_min\": 5.0, \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 1.0, \"temperature_C\": 21, \"concentration_M\": 0.1, \"BPR_bar\": 5, \"reactor_type\": \"photocoil\", \"tubing_material\": \"FEP\", \"tubing_ID_mm\": 1.0, \"reactor_volume_mL\": 5, \"residence_time_basis\": \"liquid_phase\", \"residence_time_inlet_min\": 5.0, \"residence_time_in_channel_min\": 5.0, \"light_setup\": \"420 nm LED, 100 mW/cm2 intensity, wrapped around coil\", \"wavelength_nm\": 420, \"streams\": [{\"stream_label\": \"Liquid Stream\", \"pump_role\": \"Syringe pump A\", \"contents\": \"Fmoc-L-methionine (0.1 M) and 4,7-diphenyl-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (10 mol%) in Acetonitrile\", \"solvent\": \"Acetonitrile\", \"phase\": \"liquid\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 1.0, \"concentration_M\": 0.1, \"molar_equiv\": 1.0, \"gas_flow_sccm\": 0, \"gas_flow_actual_mL_min\": 0}, {\"stream_label\": \"Gas Stream\", \"pump_role\": \"Air/O2 mass-flow controller\", \"contents\": \"Air\", \"solvent\": \"N/A\", \"phase\": \"gas\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 0, \"concentration_M\": 0, \"molar_equiv\": 0, \"gas_flow_sccm\": 50, \"gas_flow_actual_mL_min\": 2.5}], \"mixer_type\": \"Certified gas-liquid T-mixer\", \"mixing_order_reasoning\": \"Gas and liquid are mixed immediately before the reactor to maximize interfacial area for oxygen transfer during the residence time.\", \"pre_reactor_steps\": \"1. Prepare 0.1 M solution of Fmoc-L-methionine and 10 mol% photocatalyst in acetonitrile. 2. Degas acetonitrile is NOT recommended as air is the oxidant. 3. Set MFC to 50 sccm Air. 4. Set Syringe Pump to 1.0 mL/min.\", \"post_reactor_steps\": \"1. Pass through a gas-liquid separator (not in inventory, assume inline filter or vent) to remove excess air. 2. Collect product stream.\", \"chemistry_notes\": \"Batch reaction used air exposure. Flow design uses sparged air to ensure sufficient oxygen concentration. The 5 mL coil provides 5 min residence time at 1 mL/min. The 1.0 mm ID coil ensures good light penetration and gas-liquid contact.\", \"stage_parameters\": {\"mixing\": \"T-mixer at 5 bar backpressure\", \"reaction\": \"5 mL FEP coil, 420 nm LED, 21 C, 5 bar\", \"separation\": \"Inline gas-liquid separator\"}, \"reasoning_per_field\": {\"residence_time_min\": \"Matched to batch reaction time of 5 min.\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": \"1.0 mL/min is well within pump range (0.01-5.0) and provides manageable throughput.\", \"reactor_volume_mL\": \"5 mL coil selected to match 5 min residence time at 1 mL/min. 10 mL coil would double residence time, potentially over-oxidizing or requiring lower flow.\", \"gas_flow_sccm\": \"50 sccm is a conservative starting point for gas-liquid mixing in 1 mm ID tubing, ensuring excess oxygen without excessive pressure drop.\", \"BPR_bar\": \"5 bar is a safe operating pressure for FEP tubing and ensures gas remains dissolved/sparged effectively.\"}, \"literature_analogies\": \"Photo-oxidations of sulfides to sulfoxides using visible light and air are common. Flow chemistry enhances mass transfer of O2 compared to batch stirring.\", \"engine_validated\": true, \"safety_flags\": [\"Acetonitrile is flammable. Ensure no sparks near gas-liquid separator.\", \"FEP tubing is transparent to 420 nm, ensuring efficient irradiation.\", \"Pressure relief valve recommended downstream of BPR.\"], \"confidence\": 0.8}"
